{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"39703c1688caee48502791c59df99cc16ab4db0777f6c903e7118b90fbef4e95","packTokens":6724,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":6616,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"failures","tokens":39,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `POST /auth/sessions`, `GET /me/profile`, and `GET` and `POST /me/vehicles` with the request schemas, response schemas, security, and status behavior declared in the locked OpenAPI contract.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid Google identity token identifies an allowed Folio3 Google Workspace employee, and the session-creation operation has no bearer-token requirement. when The client sends the token as `googleIdentityToken` to `POST /auth/sessions`. then The response status is 201 and the returned session contains the contract-required access token, token type, expiry, employee identity, corporate email, and administrator flag.\",\n    \"Given A session request is malformed or has a missing token, or the identity token is invalid or unauthorized. when The client sends the request to `POST /auth/sessions`. then The response status is 400 for malformed or missing input, or 401 for an invalid or unauthorized identity, and the response body conforms to the contract `ApiError` schema for the applicable error.\",\n    \"Given An employee has a valid authenticated session and profile and vehicle records. when The employee requests `GET /me/profile`. then The response status is 200 and the returned profile conforms to `EmployeeProfile`, identifies the authenticated employee, and includes the contract-defined employee fields, assigned parking status, assigned floor, and vehicles; an unauthenticated request has response status 401 and an authenticated identity without permission has response status 403.\",\n    \"Given An employee has a valid authenticated session and registered vehicles. when The employee requests `GET /me/vehicles`. then The response status is 200 and the returned `vehicles` list conforms to `VehicleList` and contains only that employee's vehicles; a request without authentication has response status 401.\",\n    \"Given An employee has a valid authenticated session and submits a vehicle-registration request with a plate and optional vehicle details. when The employee sends the request to `POST /me/vehicles`. then The response status is 201 and the returned vehicle conforms to `Vehicle`, contains the submitted fields, and has status `Active`; invalid input has response status 400, missing authentication has response status 401, and a conflicting registration has response status 409, with each error response conforming to the contract `ApiError` schema.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `GET /parking/config` and `GET /parking/today` using the configured office-local date and time and contract-defined response schemas; initial office configuration uses `Asia/Karachi`, release time `08:00`, and a 30-day scheduling window.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated employee requests the office configuration and the office has its contract-example initial configuration. when The employee requests `GET /parking/config`. then The response status is 200 and the response body conforms to `ParkingConfig`, with `officeTimezone` `Asia/Karachi`, `releaseTime` `08:00`, `schedulingWindowDays` 30, working days, and the holiday setting; a request without authentication has response status 401.\",\n    \"Given An employee has a valid authenticated session and parking data for the current office-local date. when The employee requests `GET /parking/today`. then The response status is 200 and the response body conforms to `ParkingHome` and contains the office-local date and timezone, employee assignment and parking status, space status, release time, availability count, and contract-required vehicle and working-day fields; a request without authentication has response status 401.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `POST /parking/releases/today`, `GET` and `POST /parking/releases`, and `DELETE /parking/releases/{releaseId}` with contract-defined release eligibility, scheduling, filtering, cancellation, audit, and conflict behavior, calculated using the configured office-local timezone and release time.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated dedicated parking holder has a reserved space today that has not already been released or claimed. when The holder sends `POST /parking/releases/today` before or after the configured release time. then The response status is 201 and the returned release identifies the office date, `Released` status, floor, space code, and `claimableAt`; before release time `claimableAt` is the configured office-local release time, and after release time it makes the space immediately available.\",\n    \"Given A non-holder attempts a dedicated-holder release, or a holder attempts a release that conflicts with the current parking state. when The employee sends `POST /parking/releases/today`. then The response status is 403 for an ineligible employee or 409 for a conflicting state, and the response body conforms to the contract `ApiError` schema.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated dedicated holder has saved releases and supplies optional `from` and `through` date filters where applicable. when The holder requests `GET /parking/releases`. then The response status is 200 and the returned releases list conforms to `ParkingReleaseList` and contains only matching saved releases in office-local dates; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-holder receives response status 403.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated dedicated holder submits one or more valid dates within the configured scheduling window. when The holder sends those dates to `POST /parking/releases`. then The response status is 201 and the returned releases list contains one record for each accepted date with its release identifier, status, floor, space code, and `claimableAt` based on the configured office-local release time; invalid input has response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, a non-holder receives response status 403, and a conflicting release has response status 409.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated holder owns an existing unclaimed scheduled release. when The holder sends `DELETE /parking/releases/{releaseId}`. then The response status is 200 and the returned release has status `Cancelled` and includes audit events for scheduling and cancellation; missing authentication has response status 401, a non-holder receives response status 403, an unknown identifier has response status 404, and a claimed or otherwise conflicting release has response status 409.\",\n    \"Given A dedicated holder submits a malformed date or a date outside the configured scheduling window. when The holder sends the date to `POST /parking/releases`. then The response status is the contract-declared 400 for invalid input or 409 for the applicable state conflict, and the response body conforms to the contract `ApiError` schema.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `GET /parking/availability`, `POST /parking/claims`, `GET /parking/claims/today`, and `POST /parking/claims/{claimId}/cancel` with contract-defined eligibility, allocation, concurrency, response, and cancellation behavior.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated employee requests availability while released spaces are claimable. when The employee requests `GET /parking/availability`. then The response status is 200, the response body conforms to `ParkingAvailability`, and its `availableSpaceCount` equals the number of records in its spaces list, each with the contract-defined identifier, floor, and code; a request without authentication has response status 401.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated non-dedicated employee has a valid active registered vehicle and at least one claimable space. when The employee sends the vehicle ID to `POST /parking/claims`. then The response status is 201 and the returned claim conforms to `ParkingClaim` and identifies an active claim, allocated floor and space code, vehicle, authorized plate, entry status, floor capacities, and the contract allocation rule; invalid input has response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, an ineligible employee receives response status 403, and a conflicting or unavailable allocation has response status 409.\",\n    \"Given Two eligible employees request the last available space and one request is accepted first by the API. when Both employees submit valid `POST /parking/claims` requests concurrently. then The accepted response has status 201 and a returned active claim for the space, the other response has status 409, and the database contains exactly one active claim for that space.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated employee has a temporary claim for today, or has no temporary claim for today. when The employee requests `GET /parking/claims/today`. then For a claim, the response status is 200 and the returned claim conforms to `ParkingClaim` and contains its assigned space, vehicle, authorized plate, and entry status; with no claim, the response status is 404 and the response error code is `not_found`; a request without authentication has response status 401.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated employee requests cancellation of an existing active temporary claim. when The employee sends `POST /parking/claims/{claimId}/cancel`. then The response status is 409 and the returned claim remains `Active`; missing authentication has response status 401, an identity without permission receives response status 403, and an unknown claim has response status 404.\",\n    \"Given A dedicated holder requests a non-dedicated claim operation, or a non-dedicated employee requests a dedicated-holder release operation. when The API receives the relevant claim or release request. then The response status is 403 and the response body conforms to the contract `ApiError` schema.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator list operations `GET /admin/roster`, `GET /admin/entry-checks`, and `GET /admin/activity` with their contract-defined query filters, pagination, response schemas, and administrator authorization.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated parking administrator has employee roster records. when The administrator requests `GET /admin/roster` with optional search, assignment, page, and page-size parameters. then The response status is 200 and the returned page conforms to `RosterPage`, contains matching employee records with contract-defined fields, and reports page and page-count fields; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated parking administrator has recorded entrance checks. when The administrator requests `GET /admin/entry-checks` with optional search, result, and page parameters. then The response status is 200 and the returned checks conform to `EntryCheckPage`, match the supplied filters, and contain the contract-defined verification date and time, plate, result, entry status, and detail; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated parking administrator has retained parking activity. when The administrator requests `GET /admin/activity` with optional search, event type, and page parameters. then The response status is 200 and the returned events conform to `ActivityPage`, match the supplied filters and pagination, and contain the contract-defined office time, employee name, event, space or plate, and outcome; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated standard employee requests an administrator-only list operation. when The employee requests any of the roster, entry-check, or activity list routes. then The response status is 403 and the response error code is `forbidden`.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `GET /admin/utilization` to return contract-defined office-local weekly statistics and unused dedicated and temporary parking records derived from retained parking and entrance data, with administrator authorization.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated parking administrator requests a week for which parking and entrance records are available. when The administrator requests `GET /admin/utilization` with an optional `weekStart`. then The response status is 200 and the returned report conforms to `UtilizationReport` and contains the requested week dates, generation time, office timezone, released-space and temporary-claim counts, utilization percentage, daily statistics, and unused dedicated and temporary parking lists; an invalid date has response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n    \"Given A dedicated holder did not release a space and has no registered-vehicle entry record for a date, and a temporary claimant has no registered-vehicle entry record for a date. when An administrator requests the corresponding week through `GET /admin/utilization`. then The response status is 200 and the returned report lists contain the corresponding `Unused Dedicated Parking` and `Unused Temporary Parking` events with employee, vehicle plate, and office-local date.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated standard employee requests a utilization report. when The employee requests `GET /admin/utilization`. then The response status is 403 and the response error code is `forbidden`.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `GET` and `PUT /admin/settings` to read and update administrator-managed office timezone, release time, and report recipients and to return contract-defined schedule fields.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated parking administrator has office settings stored in the application database. when The administrator requests `GET /admin/settings`. then The response status is 200 and the returned `OfficeSettings` contains office timezone, release time, scheduling-window days, report recipients, report schedule, and next delivery; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated parking administrator submits valid office timezone, release time, and report-recipient values. when The administrator sends the values to `PUT /admin/settings` and then reads `GET /admin/settings`. then Both response statuses are 200 and the returned settings preserve the submitted timezone, release time, and recipient values and include the contract-defined schedule fields; invalid values have response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated standard employee submits or reads office settings. when The employee calls `PUT` or `GET /admin/settings`. then The response status is 403 and the response error code is `forbidden`.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `POST /integrations/entrance/detections` with the contract-defined request, response, security, and status behavior, recording detections and returning verification decisions without operating physical entrance hardware.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authorized integration request describes a car whose plate has an active temporary parking authorization for the office date. when The integration sends the detection to `POST /integrations/entrance/detections`. then The response status is 200 and the returned `EntranceVerification` identifies the plate as authorized, includes office date and time and contract-defined entry status, and sets `greenActivationRequested` to true.\",\n    \"Given An authorized integration request describes a car without a valid temporary allocation, a pedestrian, motorcycle, or other non-car object, or a vehicle with a permanent parking sticker. when The integration sends the detection to `POST /integrations/entrance/detections`. then The response status is 200 and the returned verification denies an unauthorized car, marks a non-car object as not applicable, or identifies a permanent sticker with entry status `Not blocked`; `greenActivationRequested` is false for each of these cases.\",\n    \"Given A detection request has valid `detectedObjectType` and `detectedAt` fields and, where applicable, a plate or failure reason. when The integration sends the request to `POST /integrations/entrance/detections`. then The response status is 200 and the response body contains the verification identifier, office date and time, plate, verification, entry status, `greenActivationRequested`, and detail; invalid input has response status 400.\",\n    \"Given A detection contains a failure reason or the verification service is unavailable. when The integration sends the detection to `POST /integrations/entrance/detections`. then The returned verification is fail-closed and requests no green activation; a verification-service outage has response status 503 and the response body conforms to `ApiError` with error code `service_unavailable`.\",\n    \"Given An integration client submits a successful or unsuccessful detection. when The API processes the detection request. then A corresponding database row records the office date and time, plate when present, verification result, and entry status.\",\n    \"Given An integration request lacks the required access token. when The API receives the detection request. then The response status is 401 and the response body conforms to `ApiError`.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall persist contract-managed employee, vehicle, parking, entrance-verification, activity, audit, configuration, and utilization records in PostgreSQL using the configured `ConnectionStrings:App` connection.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API is configured through `ConnectionStrings:App` with an isolated PostgreSQL database, and a test creates its own employee, vehicle, and parking fixtures with demo seeding disabled. when The test registers a vehicle, schedules a release, claims a space, records an entrance detection, updates office settings, restarts the API, and reads the corresponding records through the API and database. then The selected PostgreSQL database contains a row for each persisted operation, and the returned vehicle, release, claim, verification, and settings values remain available after restart.\",\n    \"Given A client successfully creates a vehicle or parking record through a contract operation using the configured PostgreSQL database. when The API is restarted and the client reads the record using the corresponding API operation. then The PostgreSQL database contains the corresponding row and the response returns the persisted record.\",\n    \"Given A client successfully updates settings, creates a claim, or submits an entrance detection. when The corresponding API operation completes. then A PostgreSQL row contains the saved configuration, claim, or verification record and its contract-defined identifiers and values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When `Seed:Demo` is true, the API shall run demo seeding by inserting sample records using contract example values only when their contract-defined identifiers are absent and never overwriting or deleting existing records; when `Seed:Demo` is false, startup makes no demo inserts.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A fresh PostgreSQL database has `Seed:Demo=false` or the setting is unset. when The API starts and a contract-backed table is inspected for demo sample identifiers. then The database row count for demo sample identifiers is zero.\",\n    \"Given A PostgreSQL database contains a record whose contract-defined identifier matches a demo record and `Seed:Demo=true`. when The API starts twice against that database. then The existing row values remain unchanged and the database contains no duplicate demo identifier.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When demo seeding is enabled, the API shall insert at least two sample rows in each contract-backed table using values from contract examples.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A fresh PostgreSQL database has `Seed:Demo=true` and contract examples are available as seed sources. when The API starts and its contract-backed tables are inspected. then Each contract-backed table contains at least two sample rows using values from contract examples.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When demo seeding is enabled, the API shall insert three sample records in each repeatable contract-backed data table and one record in the singleton office-settings table, using business-field values based on contract examples.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A fresh PostgreSQL database has demo configuration available. when The public `SeedData.Run` method is called directly. then The database row count is three for each repeatable contract-backed data table and one for the singleton office-settings table, and saved field values are based on contract examples.\",\n    \"Given The API starts with `Seed:Demo=true` and demo employee and administrator identities are authenticated. when The clients call contract collection operations, including vehicles, releases, availability, roster, entry checks, utilization, and activity. then Each response is successful and each returned collection or report list has a count of at least one.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When `Seed:Demo` is true, the API shall insert between two and five contract-example-derived sample records for each contract-backed table.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A fresh PostgreSQL database has `Seed:Demo=true`. when The API starts and its contract-backed tables are inspected. then Each table has between two and five sample rows whose values are derived from the corresponding contract examples.\",\n    \"Given A fresh PostgreSQL database has `Seed:Demo=false` and no test fixtures are created. when The API starts and an employee requests their releases. then The response status is 200 with an empty returned release list, and the database contains no demo sample rows.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The API shall publish all 21 operations declared in `contracts/openapi.yaml` with their declared paths, methods, request and response schemas, security, parameters, and status behavior without implementing employee-facing parking-product screens in this API project.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API is running with its published OpenAPI document enabled. when A client requests `GET /openapi/v1.json`. then The response status is 200 and the returned document lists all 21 contract paths and methods with declared request, response, and security metadata and no employee-facing parking-product screen route.\",\n    \"Given A client sends a request to any documented contract operation. when The API processes the contract-defined request. then The response content type is `application/json` and the response body conforms to that operation's declared response schema rather than a parking-product screen.\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": []\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L8 anchors] REQ-9 has an anchor that doesn't match the code\n</failures>\n\nRestate the change."}